{"id": "11th_tamil_u1_q019", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "multiple_choice", "level": "hard", "difficulty": "hard", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "11", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "unit_1", "lesson_id": "prose_speech_and_poem", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "match_thinkers", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "பொருத்துக:\n(a) பால் வலேரி - 1. மனிதன் ஒரு குறியீட்டு விலங்கு\n(b) ஸ்டெபான் மல்லார்மே - 2. கவிதை என்பது நடனம், உரைநடை நடை\n(c) ஏர்னஸ்ட் காசிரர் - 3. புல்லின் இதழ்கள்\n(d) வால்ட் விட்மன் - 4. கவிதை சொற்களால் இயற்றப்படுவது", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "(a)-1, (b)-4, (c)-2, (d)-3", "B": "(a)-4, (b)-2, (c)-1, (d)-3", "C": "(a)-2, (b)-4, (c)-1, (d)-3", "D": "(a)-3, (b)-1, (c)-4, (d)-2"}, "explanation": "பால் வலேரி = கவிதை நடனம், உரைநடை நடை; மல்லார்மே = கவிதை சொற்களால் ஆனது; காசிரர் = குறியீட்டு விலங்கு; விட்மன் = புல்லின் இதழ்கள். எனவே விடை C."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Match the thinkers with their key ideas/works:\n(a) Paul Valery - 1. Man is a symbolic animal\n(b) Stephane Mallarme - 2. Poetry is dance, prose is walk\n(c) Ernst Cassirer - 3. Leaves of Grass\n(d) Walt Whitman - 4. Poetry is made of words", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "(a)-1, (b)-4, (c)-2, (d)-3", "B": "(a)-4, (b)-2, (c)-1, (d)-3", "C": "(a)-2, (b)-4, (c)-1, (d)-3", "D": "(a)-3, (b)-1, (c)-4, (d)-2"}, "explanation": "Valery = Dance/Walk; Mallarme = Words; Cassirer = Symbolic Animal; Whitman = Leaves of Grass."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "C", "accepted_keys": ["C"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "11", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 3, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "11th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 3", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["Class 11", "Unit 1", "Prose", "Matching"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T12:00:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T12:00:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "11th_tamil_u1_q020", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "multiple_choice", "level": "medium", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "11", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "unit_1", "lesson_id": "prose_speech_and_poem", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "neruda_quote", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "‘சொற்கள்தான் எங்களை வழிநடத்துகின்றன, சொற்கள்தான் உலகை வெளிப்படுத்துகின்றன’ என்று சொற்களின் பேராற்றலை வியந்து கூறியவர் யார்?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "கதே", "B": "ஷேக்ஸ்பியர்", "C": "மில்டன்", "D": "பாப்லோ நெருடா"}, "explanation": "சிலி நாட்டுக் கவிஞர் பாப்லோ நெருடா சொற்களின் மாயாஜால ஆற்றலையும் மனித வாழ்வை அவை இயக்கும் தன்மையையும் வியந்து பாடியுள்ளார்."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Who marveled at the supreme power of words saying 'Words lead us and words illuminate the universe'?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Goethe", "B": "Shakespeare", "C": "Milton", "D": "Pablo Neruda"}, "explanation": "Pablo Neruda celebrated how words guide human consciousness and render reality visible."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "D", "accepted_keys": ["D"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "11", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 4, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "11th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 4", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["Class 11", "Unit 1", "Prose", "Pablo Neruda"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T12:00:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T12:00:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "11th_tamil_u1_q021", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "multiple_choice", "level": "medium", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "11", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "unit_1", "lesson_id": "prose_speech_and_poem", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "modern_art", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "கவிஞர் இந்திரனின் திறனாய்வுப் பார்வை பெரும்பாலும் எந்த கலைத் துறையோடு தமிழ்க் கவிதையை இணைத்துப் பார்க்கிறது?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "நவீன ஓவியம் மற்றும் காட்சி அழகியல்", "B": "கிரேக்கக் கட்டிடக்கலை", "C": "கர்நாடக சங்கீதம்", "D": "பரதநாட்டிய அடவுகள்"}, "explanation": "இந்திரன் ஒரு புகழ்பெற்ற கலை விமர்சகர் என்பதால், நவீன ஓவியக் கோட்பாடுகள், காட்சிக் குறியீடுகள் மற்றும் நவீன அழகியல் சார்ந்து தமிழ்க் கவிதைகளை நுட்பமாகப் பகுப்பாய்வு செய்கிறார்."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "With which artistic discipline does poet Indiran frequently correlate modern Tamil poetry in his critical essays?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Modern painting and visual aesthetics", "B": "Greek architecture", "C": "Carnatic classical music", "D": "Bharatanatyam movements"}, "explanation": "As a renowned modern art critic, Indiran links poetic imagery with contemporary painting and visual aesthetics."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "A", "accepted_keys": ["A"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation"